    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Battle of Plassey (1757) laid the foundation of British political power in India.",
        "The victory in the Battle of Buxar (1764) resulted in the landmark Treaty of Allahabad in 1765.",
        "Administrative policies like the Subsidiary Alliance and Doctrine of Lapse served as key mechanisms for territorial annexation.",
        "Economic policies introduced under various Governors-General significantly reshaped the Indian socio-economic landscape."
